      "id": 444155,
      "username": "thinkdigital",
      "name": "Think Digital",
      "created_at": "2024-11-02T13:00:31.420Z",
      "cooked": "<h1><a name=\"p-444155-public-vs-private-bench-groups-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-444155-public-vs-private-bench-groups-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Public vs Private Bench Groups</h1>\n<h2><a name=\"p-444155-private-bench-groups-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-444155-private-bench-groups-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>Private Bench Groups</h2>\n<p>In contrast to public / managed bench groups, private bench groups <strong>are under your control</strong>. You get to choose what apps to add (yup, you can add your own custom apps too!), what apps to update, what region to deploy onto, SSH Access, Server scripts (v15+) etc are only available in a private bench group.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://docs.frappe.io/cloud/benches\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://docs.frappe.io/files/cloud.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/cloud/benches\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">docs.frappe.io</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    \n\n<h3><a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/cloud/benches\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Private Bench Groups</a></h3>\n\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/thinkdigital/{size}/74170_2.png",
